Description:
    Generates a reactive CRUD resource for a model that ALREADY exists — the
    overlay half of hibiki:rails:scaffold.

    With no field list the model's own schema is read: columns and types,
    belongs_to reflections, and the validators behind per-field live errors.
    Pass fields explicitly to override that, or when the table has not been
    migrated yet.

    The generated index is live: search, filter, sort and pagination are signal
    state, edits happen in place, and a write from anywhere repaints every open
    list.

    Two models are MODIFIED. This one gets a delegate per belongs_to plus the
    after_commit broadcast the whole thing hangs off; each model a belongs_to
    POINTS AT gets the has_many half Rails' scaffold never writes, and a ping,
    because a row prints the parent's label rather than its id. Both are
    idempotent, both are announced, and anything already declared is left alone.

Example:
    bin/rails generate hibiki:rails:scaffold_controller Book

    This will create:
        app/models/book_query.rb
        app/models/book_row.rb
        app/channels/books_channel.rb
        app/channels/book_channel.rb
        app/forms/book_form.rb
        app/controllers/books_controller.rb
        app/views/books/*
        app/assets/stylesheets/hibiki_busy.css
    And modify:
        app/models/book.rb
        app/models/author.rb   # each model a belongs_to points at
        config/routes.rb

    Pass --phlex to emit Phlex components under app/views/books/*.rb instead of
    ERB templates. The view layer is the only thing it changes; it needs the
    phlex-rails gem and `bin/rails g phlex:install`.
